WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:05.160
From death by power washer to a&nbsp;
murderous "doom dance," these are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:08.793
the wild M3GAN moments that will keep&nbsp;
you up at night for weeks to come.

00:00:08.793 --> 00:00:11.580
One of the joys in any robot-centric film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:17.520
horror or otherwise, is seeing the android getting&nbsp;
assembled. A prime example of this is the opening&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:22.560
title sequence of Short Circuit, which takes&nbsp;
ample time to show the construction of Johnny 5.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:25.200
"Hello, bozos!"

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:29.820
Early on in M3GAN we're introduced to Gemma&nbsp;
and the fancy toy company she works for,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:33.420
the Funki Company. Funki is shown to&nbsp;
specialize in highly sophisticated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:38.940
robotic toys, most famously a Hatchimals and&nbsp;
Furby-like hybrid known as a Perpetual Pet.

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:43.320
However, it's quickly shown that Gemma and&nbsp;
two of her cronies have bigger plans in mind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:47.820
much to their boss David's chagrin.&nbsp;
Their initial demo doesn't go as planned,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:52.080
with the prototype M3GAN glitching out.&nbsp;
It's here that we get to see M3GAN in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:56.340
early stages of her construction, still&nbsp;
missing many of her key visual features.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.340 --> 00:01:01.140
With her exposed metallic skull being&nbsp;
outfitted with its flesh-like exterior,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:07.440
it even conjures up memories of the Child's Play&nbsp;
2 title sequence. Seeing M3GAN in this unfinished,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:13.541
borderline skeletal state is more than a little&nbsp;
bit creepy, and a solid omen of what's to come.

00:01:13.541 --> 00:01:15.240
From the moment M3GAN is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:20.220
fully constructed, it doesn't take too long for&nbsp;
things to go from zero to creepy. We see that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:24.840
following a conversation with her niece Cady,&nbsp;
Gemma is driven to improve the prototype robot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:29.640
she'd previously shown her boss. Cady, upon&nbsp;
seeing an old robot of Gemma's named Bruce,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:34.200
notes that if she had something like it&nbsp;
she'd likely never need another toy. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:39.540
results in Gemma giving her invention a complete&nbsp;
top-to-bottom overhaul, designed to be just right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:45.300
for Cady and potentially other children. This&nbsp;
eventually results in the fully finished M3GAN,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:49.440
complete with fashionable clothes&nbsp;
and a cute — if uncanny — face.

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:54.600
Upon their admittedly very bizarre introduction&nbsp;
to each other, M3GAN quickly pairs with Cady&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:59.460
as her primary user. It's during this sequence&nbsp;
we are given a taste of M3GAN's point-of-view,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:04.680
a recurring motif throughout the film. In an&nbsp;
instant, M3GAN makes Cady's happiness her number&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:10.020
one goal. Certainly nothing unsettling about that&nbsp;
... right? It's a moment that's disturbing due to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:15.764
the film's premise, meaning that you, the viewer,&nbsp;
know already that this can only end badly.

00:02:15.764 --> 00:02:17.820
It doesn't take too long for things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:22.920
to get creepy with M3GAN, as it becomes clear that&nbsp;
she takes her programming a little too seriously.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:28.200
After pairing with Cady, maintaining her happiness&nbsp;
and well-being soon becomes a consistent mission&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:33.120
for M3GAN. At first it seems innocent enough, as&nbsp;
it appears that M3GAN is meeting her objective&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:38.280
with flying colors. She successfully dazzles&nbsp;
Gemma's boss and a room of potential product&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:43.620
investors during an in-house presentation.&nbsp;
Then, M3GAN and Cady begin playing constantly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:48.180
with Cady taking more and more of a shine to&nbsp;
her new robotic companion as the days go on.

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:51.840
However, it seems that M3GAN has&nbsp;
taken a major shine to Cady as well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:57.120
going as far as to watch her as she sleeps.&nbsp;
This is one of the first signs that M3GAN&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:02.580
is starting to go wrong, as this is the time&nbsp;
she should be offline recharging. We've seen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:08.016
variations on this moment in other movies,&nbsp;
most recently the 2019 Child's Play reboot.

00:03:08.016 --> 00:03:10.416
"You're my best friend Andy."

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:14.280
That film already proved that&nbsp;
placing an unchecked artificial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:18.180
intelligence in a children's toy&nbsp;
is a bad idea. Needless to say,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:22.650
M3GAN does a pretty good job in this film&nbsp;
of giving Chucky a run for his money.

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:25.320
You never mess with someone's BFF,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:29.940
especially when that someone is an&nbsp;
unstable android with rapidly evolving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:34.560
killing capabilities. The catalyst for the film's&nbsp;
events are set in motion when Cady's parents are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:38.400
killed in a car accident. This leaves her&nbsp;
in the care of Gemma, her mother's sister,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:43.680
who must now serve as her guardian. As part of&nbsp;
this newfound arrangement, a child therapist makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:48.780
semi-regular visits to see how Cady is adjusting.&nbsp;
The first visit serves to show the audience just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:53.280
how unprepared Gemma is as a new guardian,&nbsp;
not really knowing how to interact with Cady.

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:58.860
However, the awkwardness of this encounter is&nbsp;
upstaged by the therapist's next visit, when M3GAN&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:04.920
is present. The therapist's very serious line of&nbsp;
questioning quickly upsets Cady, bringing her to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:11.280
tears, much to M3GAN's very heated disapproval.&nbsp;
M3GAN then proceeds to threaten the therapist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:17.965
simply telling her, "You made [Cady] cry," which&nbsp;
understandably unsettles both adults in the room.

00:04:17.965 --> 00:04:20.820
The film's climax truly kicks off on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:26.580
night of M3GAN's intended public unveiling, which&nbsp;
is where everything goes completely sideways. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:31.800
at this point of the film that Gemma finally steps&nbsp;
up in terms of her guardianship of Cady. Following&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:36.420
a heated conversation, Gemma opts to dip out on&nbsp;
the highly touted presentation to drive Cady home&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:41.280
and put her to bed. During this time, M3GAN is&nbsp;
restrained in a harness prior to her unveiling,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:45.420
being prepped by Gemma's coworkers, Cole&nbsp;
and Tess. However, as things start to go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:49.560
on the fritz it soon becomes clear to them&nbsp;
that something is very wrong with M3GAN.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:54.300
Before they can successfully unplug her, M3GAN&nbsp;
launches her counterattack, starting by tying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:58.920
Cole up in her restraints. She's then able to&nbsp;
intercept a phone call intended to warn Gemma,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:03.780
who's currently in transit with Cady. M3GAN then&nbsp;
releases some gas and sets off an explosion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:08.520
setting Gemma's workspace ablaze with&nbsp;
Cole and Tess inside. It's from here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:12.900
that M3GAN begins her epic rampage&nbsp;
that makes up the film's final act.

00:05:13.407 --> 00:05:15.507
"It's insane, right?"

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:21.300
From the minute the trailer for M3GAN dropped,&nbsp;
there was no escaping this utterly meme-worthy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:27.180
moment. As the film settles in for its third act,&nbsp;
M3GAN fully solidifies her psychopathic turn by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:32.160
going berserk ahead of her public unveiling. Not&nbsp;
only does she assault Gemma's coworkers, nearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:37.500
scorching them alive, but then goes after Gemma's&nbsp;
boss David as well. As David marches the hallway,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:44.280
miffed over Gemma's premature departure, M3GAN&nbsp;
makes her presence known in a big bad way. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:50.160
chases David down and as she glides through the&nbsp;
hallway, proceeds to bust into a bizarre dance.

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:54.060
While this moment is still&nbsp;
disturbing in a darkly humorous way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.060 --> 00:05:58.980
there's no denying that the scene&nbsp;
is just that — humorous. Granted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.980 --> 00:06:04.260
this does culminate in David's gruesome demise,&nbsp;
but the buildup to it is a supremely campy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:09.360
moment in an already campy movie. M3GAN&nbsp;
has a solid balance of horror and humor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:15.224
often to simultaneously great effect, but this&nbsp;
moment definitely leans heavier into the comedy.

00:06:15.224 --> 00:06:16.500
The film's finale&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:21.900
is a true nail-biter, as it seems that nothing&nbsp;
can really stop M3GAN, who just keeps coming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:26.640
with relentless tenacity. But despite the&nbsp;
robot's best efforts, with Cady's help,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:31.920
Gemma is able to finally put M3GAN down for&nbsp;
good just as the cops arrive. Not only that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:37.560
but it's shown that her coworkers, clearly a bit&nbsp;
worse for wear, also survived. This allows an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:43.080
exhausted Gemma to take Cady and finally depart,&nbsp;
leaving their technological nightmare behind.

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:49.020
All seems to be wrapped up in a neat little bow&nbsp;
— that is, until we see Gemma's Siri-like home&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:54.120
assistant come back online. Much like other&nbsp;
great slasher villains like Chucky or Jason,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:58.620
it appears that M3GAN might have been able&nbsp;
to cheat her demise in haunting fashion.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:03.060
Whether or not this will lead to an '80s&nbsp;
slasher-style sequel remains to be seen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:05.545
but it certainly wouldn't be unwelcome.

00:07:05.545 --> 00:07:08.400
Early on in M3GAN, we're shown that Gemma has to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:13.680
deal with a rather nosy neighbor who has a rather&nbsp;
annoying dog. At first, it's shown that Gemma has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:18.180
to constantly tell her neighbor to keep the dog&nbsp;
off of her property. After Cady and M3GAN have a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:24.480
run-in with the dog, the pesky canine soon ends up&nbsp;
in M3GAN's cybernetic crosshairs. M3GAN dispatches&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:29.160
the dog off-screen, causing the neighbor to&nbsp;
immediately point a finger at Cady and Gemma.

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:33.300
Despite police intervention, there's nothing&nbsp;
to really connect them to it beyond the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:37.620
previous incident, much to the neighbor's&nbsp;
annoyance. Not one to leave loose ends,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.620 --> 00:07:42.480
M3GAN sets her sights on the neighbor, and&nbsp;
makes her move later that night. She hides&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:47.400
in the neighbors shed and, after emerging from&nbsp;
the darkness, attacks her in a gruesome fashion.

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:53.100
M3GAN must be a fan of Fede Alvarez's Evil&nbsp;
Dead, because she uses a nail gun to subdue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.100 --> 00:07:57.960
the neighbor. Never one to do something halfway,&nbsp;
she then proceeds to grab a pressure washer the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.960 --> 00:08:01.800
neighbor was seen using earlier. This is&nbsp;
more than enough to fully put her down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.800 --> 00:08:08.136
making for a gloriously disturbing sequence and&nbsp;
a true showcase of how dangerous M3GAN can be.

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:12.360
Gemma's boss David, played by senior&nbsp;
Daily Show correspondent Ronny Chieng,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:17.460
provides comic relief throughout the film with&nbsp;
his jerk tech mogul persona. It's a character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:22.320
that in lesser hands could've been stock and&nbsp;
annoying, but Chieng definitely makes the role&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:26.880
his own. This makes his eventual demise all the&nbsp;
more disturbing and even a little bit hilarious,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:31.680
a balance the film handles quite well.&nbsp;
Following her now meme-worthy dance of doom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:35.100
Megan takes off in hot pursuit&nbsp;
of David. Fortunately for him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:39.540
escape is in sight as the elevator at the end&nbsp;
of the hall opens up with his assistant inside.

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:43.980
But the assistant, having been thoroughly&nbsp;
mistreated by David throughout the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.980 --> 00:08:48.180
quickly begins pushing the elevator's&nbsp;
"close" button. This allows M3GAN to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:53.520
catch up and gruesomely dispatch David before&nbsp;
turning her attention to the assistant. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.520 --> 00:08:58.320
notes his mistreatment under David and how&nbsp;
he'll make the perfect cover for this murder,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.320 --> 00:09:03.780
thinking three steps ahead as always. Both&nbsp;
men's bodies are found in the elevator,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.780 --> 00:09:09.585
horrifying those in attendance for the unveiling&nbsp;
and allowing M3GAN to hijack a car and ride off.

00:09:09.585 --> 00:09:11.400
After some steady buildup,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:16.800
M3GAN finally shows just how dangerous she can&nbsp;
be when Cady is bothered by a bully during a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:21.180
school trip. Upon being dropped off, one of the&nbsp;
adults chaperoning notices M3GAN in the car and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:26.280
asks what she is. After Gemma explains that she's&nbsp;
a toy, Cady is allowed to keep M3GAN with her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.280 --> 00:09:30.180
although she must be left with the other&nbsp;
kids' toys and belongings. But soon enough,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.180 --> 00:09:35.280
Cady soon finds herself being abused by a rather&nbsp;
nasty kid named Brandon, neither child aware&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:39.420
of the degree to which Cady's happiness&nbsp;
and protection is M3GAN's main objective.

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:44.220
In a flash, M3GAN attacks Brandon and&nbsp;
goes as far as to rip his ear off,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.220 --> 00:09:49.260
throwing it into the woods. Brandon runs&nbsp;
and M3GAN gives chase, entering some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.260 --> 00:09:53.402
form of attack mode where she gets on all&nbsp;
fours and pursues him like a wild animal.

00:09:55.123 --> 00:09:56.503
"You should probably run."

00:09:56.503 --> 00:10:01.620
M3GAN herself doesn't get to finish off Brandon,&nbsp;
as in his escape he stumbles into the road where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:06.900
he's then hit by a car. M3GAN then later&nbsp;
informs Cady, in rather disturbing fashion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.900 --> 00:10:11.766
that Brandon will not be going to heaven&nbsp;
and that no one will ever hurt her again.

00:10:11.766 --> 00:10:14.220
The closing moments of M3GAN truly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:16.980
make for some of the film's&nbsp;
most enthralling moments,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.980 --> 00:10:22.560
as the climax makes every second count. Upon&nbsp;
arriving home, Gemma is confronted by M3GAN,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:27.960
who firmly dispossesess any pretense of being&nbsp;
friendly towards her. She even goes as far as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:33.660
to say that Gemma "shouldn't be a mom," just&nbsp;
as one last kick in the gut. Cady emerges to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:38.040
see M3GAN attacking Gemma, finally seeing&nbsp;
her robotic "friend" in all of her true&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:43.560
homicidal glory. This results in M3GAN's&nbsp;
movements becoming more erratic and creepy.

00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:47.100
After attacking Cady and Gemma, it&nbsp;
seems that M3GAN is harder to put&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:51.480
down than a T-800. All joking aside, the&nbsp;
parallels to The Terminator are blatant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.480 --> 00:10:56.760
right down to M3GAN's human-like exterior slowly&nbsp;
being eroded throughout the final fight. Just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.760 --> 00:11:02.520
as it seems like Gemma is doomed, Cady takes&nbsp;
control of Bruce, Gemma's old prototype robot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.520 --> 00:11:07.440
to begin whoopping M3GAN like a ragdoll.&nbsp;
But even this isn't enough to put M3GAN&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.440 --> 00:11:13.260
down for good, leaving Gemma to finish her off&nbsp;
by plunging a screwdriver into M3GAN's "brain."

